<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indo-Fijians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indo-Fijians are Fijian citizens of Indian descent, most of them descended from about 60,000 indentured labourers brought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> between 1879 and 1916 to work on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations. By the 1940s they outnumbered indigenous Fijians, but most land remained reserved for Fijian communities. Political tensions led to the coups of 1987 and 2000, after which many Indo-Fijians emigrated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indo-fijians.jpg" alt="Indo-Fijians" width="320" height="298" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CrimsonMagma · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethnic_Map_of_Fiji.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
